course: dictionary
lesson: 15996
title: Vacate: leave a place empty
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Vacate is a formal word, so you will often see it on signs and notices. To vacate a place means to leave it so that it is empty for someone else. «Please vacate the room by eleven o'clock.» The clue is the time: the room must be empty by then so someone else can use it.
explain: You can also vacate a job or a seat. «She vacated her seat for the old man on the bus.» She got up and gave her seat up so the old man could sit in it. Here vacate means give up, not just walk out.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in a simpler word. «Please leave the room by eleven o'clock» still makes sense, so leave is a close match. Vacate is more formal, and it often suggests that the place is left empty. «Everyone must vacate the building» in a fire drill means every person must get out.
fact: Vacate is a verb: vacate, vacates, vacated, vacating.
fact: To vacate a place means to leave it so that it is empty for someone else.
fact: To vacate a job or seat means to give it up.
fact: Vacate is a formal word, so you will often see it in hotels, flats, offices and on notices.
fact: A related word is «vacant», which means empty, as in «a vacant seat».
exercise: «Please vacate the room by eleven o'clock.» What does vacate mean here? | Decorate it with flowers for a party | *Leave it so it is empty | Lock it and keep the key | Clean it from top to bottom
exercise: «When the alarm rings, everyone must vacate the building.» What should people do? | Ring the alarm again | Hide under the desks | *Leave the building | Stay inside and wait for the all-clear
exercise: «He vacated his job last year.» What does vacated mean? | *Gave the job up | Started work early | Asked for a pay rise | Got a new job for more money
test: «The guests must vacate their rooms before noon.» What does vacate mean? | Make the bed and tidy the room | *Leave the room so it is empty | Stay for one more night | Lock the door and keep the key
test: Tom says vacate means «to clean up». What is the correct meaning? | *Leave a place so it is empty for someone else | Enter a place quietly | Clean the place with a mop | Decorate a place for a party
exam: «She decided to vacate her seat for the old man.» What does vacate mean here? | Break it | Sit down in it | *Give it up so someone else can have it | Stay in it
